#### 📄 **Code: `main.cpp`**
```cpp
#include <SFML/Graphics.hpp>

int main() {
    // Create the window (width, height, title)
    sf::RenderWindow window(sf::VideoMode(1280, 720), "Death Circuit");

    // Set the frame rate limit to 120 FPS
    window.setFramerateLimit(120);

    // Main game loop (runs until the window is closed)
    while (window.isOpen()) {
        sf::Event event;

        // Process all events (keyboard, mouse, close)
        while (window.pollEvent(event)) {
            if (event.type == sf::Event::Closed) {
                window.close(); // click “X” closes window
            }
        }

        // Fill the window with a dark background color
        window.clear(sf::Color(10, 10, 15));

        // Draw goes here (for now nothing yet)

        // Show the rendered frame on screen
        window.display();
    }

    return 0;
}
```

---

#### 🧠 **Explanation Line-by-Line**

| Code | What It Does |
|------|---------------|
| `#include <SFML/Graphics.hpp>` | Pulls in SFML’s graphics library — gives you access to windows, shapes, images, etc. |
| `sf::RenderWindow window(...)` | Creates a window where the game runs. You can set resolution, name, and fullscreen later. |
| `window.setFramerateLimit(120);` | Limits frame rate — avoids your GPU spinning at 1000 FPS. |
| `while (window.isOpen())` | The **main game loop** — runs every frame until you exit. |
| `sf::Event event; while(window.pollEvent(event))` | Handles all input and OS messages (close, resize, keypress). |
| `window.clear(...)` | Erases last frame with a solid color so we can draw fresh. |
| `window.display();` | Pushes everything you drew this frame to the screen. |

Right now it just opens a blank black window — perfect base.

